      "problem": "There are $98$ blue marbles and some red marbles in a box. The ratio of the number of blue marbles to the number of red ones is $2:1.$ By rounding the number of blue marbles to the nearest ten, approximate the number of red marbles in the box.",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's approximate the number of blue marbles:\n\n$$\n98⟶100\n$$\n\nThe ratio of the number of blue marbles to the number of red marbles is\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{1}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe numerator represents the number of blue marbles and the denominator represents the number of red marbles.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $100$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by \n $50:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{2\\times 50}{1\\times 50}=\\frac{100}{50}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are approximately $50$ red marbles in the box.",
